<title>BRAZIL: Brazil June 6 coffee regs 2.32 mln bags to August.</title>
<headline>Brazil June 6 coffee regs 2.32 mln bags to August.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil coffee sales registrations as of June 6 totalled 2.32 million 60-kg bags for June, July and August, according to the June 12 bulletin of the Rio de Janeiro Coffee Center.</p>
<p>Of this, 1.32 million bags had been registered for June.</p>
<p>Stronger-than-expected export performance led the government last week to request exporters to make no more new sales for June and delay June shipments into July as much as possible.</p>
<p>The government's concern is due to an export limit of six million bags between January and June this year, agreed with other producing countries.</p>
<p>However by the end of May, Brazil had already shipped 6.46 million bags and some traders have said they expect further shipments of up to 1.4 million bags this month.</p>
<p>A breakdown by month was as follows.</p>
<p> MONTH     REGISTRATIONS IN 60-KG BAGS</p>
<p> June		   1,321,875</p>
<p> July		     848,540</p>
<p> August		   154,120</p>
<p> TOTAL		  2,324,535</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
